    "AI Notes": {
      "value": "FIELD.IO is a London/Berlin creative technology and generative art studio founded in 2009 by Marcus Wendt and Vera-Maria Glahn. Studio-level autonomy (5): they originate and lead their own projects, with long-running client partnerships including IBM, Nike, Meta, Google, and Chopard. LinkedIn lists 11-50 employees; 2016 coverage cited a team of 12, with Berlin expansion since, so 11-40 is a reasonable current read. Work spans AI-powered installations, generative brand systems, immersive retail environments, data visualisation, spatial/experiential design, and motion. Not individually credited freelancers but a full integrated studio; seniority read is creative direction and execution under one roof.",
